From: Codex M2 runtime compatibility
Subject: [PATCH] Finalize existing CACHE metadata bind and flagless VNDK33 container

Reason: final vendor restore removed the fork's /cache/metadata bind. A37 manifest
flag parsing then omits RANGING and AppOps crashes. Reinstate the existing bind in
canonical hw init after the restore; mirror donor metadata labels at the CACHE
path to survive core restorecon/cache. Represent the legacy vendor's actual zero
aconfig flags with a valid empty v2 container, avoiding donor hardware flags.
Files: existing boot_restore finalization, two Python helpers, M1/M2 profiles.
Enable only reviewed star2lte/A376B M2; M1 resets the opt-in. No new build system,
partition, kernel or hardware/radio blob replacement. Unknown nonempty vendor
storage is refused. Generated files are not stored as firmware in this patch.
Verify: idempotence/anchor rejection, upstream AOSP Java storage readers, actual
G965F two-boot CACHE inode/hash persistence, labels/flags/RANGING and Enforcing;
platform aconfigd exits0 with the empty vendor container. See runtime report.
Rollback: reverse patch/rebuild or restore exact rc/context files, remove only
newly generated container files and restore original BOOT on the test phone.

